---
import Layout from "@/layouts/main.astro"
import { SITE } from "@/lib/site"
---

<Layout
  seo={{
    title: "Privacy | Cybotum",
    description:
      "Read how the Cybotum starter handles privacy, contact messages, and optional third-party tools.",
    canonical: "/privacy",
  }}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 md:py-20">
    <article class="space-y-10">
      <header class="max-w-2xl">
        <span class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-muted-foreground">
          Legal
        </span>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-5xl">Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground md:text-lg">
          This policy describes the default privacy posture of the starter template. Update it if
          you add analytics, forms, email capture, or other third-party services.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What the starter collects</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
          By default, the site is static and does not require accounts, databases, or server-side
          form handling. If a visitor contacts you by email, that message is handled by their email
          provider and any mail system you use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Third-party services</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
          You may add external services for analytics, fonts, embeds, or hosting later. If you do,
          update this policy so it reflects the actual data flow in your deployed project.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
          Questions about privacy or the template setup can be sent to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="font-medium text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">
            {SITE.email}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
